<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46140" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subter-lābor</span></b> ,
		lābi, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>v. dep. n.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>to glide</i> or <i>flow under</i> (mostly <b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fluctus Sicanos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 10, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flumina subterlabentia muros,</span>”
				<i>flowing close by</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. G.
					2, 157</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subterlabens Mosella,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 10, 21</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to slip away</i>,
				<i>escape</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">celeritate subterlabentem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					30, 25</span></i>
			 (dub.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
